    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.11_base_commutative_diagram.chapters.04_history_and_path_admission.sections.01_history_motivation.concrete_anchor_16_PathLawhceqgfc#pathlaw_h_c_eq_g_f_c" .
silm:instances_papers_11_base_commutative_diagram_chapters_04_history_and_path_admission_sections_01_history_motivation_concrete_anchor_16_PathLawhceqgfc#pathlaw_h_c_eq_g_f_c silm:hasLongDescription "The PathLaw_h_c_eq_g_f_c is the commuting path equation: direct Animal leg equals the Cat->Mammal->Animal composite. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'PathLaw_h_c_eq_g_f_c', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
